    "b887488c6c": {
      "id": "b887488c6c",
      "created": 1795068609.5957644,
      "headline": "GTA 6 Personal Vehicles: How to Register, Store and Recover Your Ride",
      "url": "https://www.gamesradar.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-personal-vehicles-how-to-register-switch-recover-car/",
      "source": "GamesRadar+",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068604/gta-bot/b887488c6c-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068604/gta-bot/b887488c6c-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068605/gta-bot/b887488c6c-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068606/gta-bot/b887488c6c-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068607/gta-bot/b887488c6c-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068609/gta-bot/b887488c6c-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Your ride just got a safety net. 🚗 In GTA 6, a Personal Vehicle is one you've paid to register, and if it's wrecked, the ScooterBros app can bring it back for a fee. Unowned cars get no such deal, and anything in their trunk is lost if they're destroyed. Swipe for how to register, store and recover your wheels.\n\nWhich car are you registering first?\n\nSource: GamesRadar+\n\n#GTA6 #GTAVI #GrandTheftAutoVI #Leonida #RockstarGames #GTA6Guide #GTA6Tips #PersonalVehicle #ScooterBros #GamingNews",
      "alt_text": "Graphic with the headline 'GTA 6 Personal Vehicles: How to Register, Store and Recover Your Ride' and a GUIDE label.",
      "score": 7,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "GUIDE",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "What is a Personal Vehicle?",
          "text": "It's a car or bike you're legally registered to ride. Its location is always marked on the map, under the Personal tab of the Index. Its trunk lets you manage your loadout, change outfits and store stash bags."
        },
        {
          "title": "How to register one",
          "text": "Drive an unowned vehicle to a Pay 'n' Spray and pay the fee, which depends on the make and model. Extra registered vehicles need extra garage space. ScooterBros can summon any of them for a fee."
        },
        {
          "title": "Unowned vehicles and wrecks",
          "text": "You can steal almost any car, but unowned ones can't be recovered once destroyed, and their trunk contents are lost. Park them outside your safehouse or in a garage to keep them safe."
        },
        {
          "title": "Impounded? Here's the fix",
          "text": "Dumping your car can clear Vehicle Heat, but cops will likely impound it. ScooterBros can fetch it for a hefty fee, though stash bags in the trunk may be lost. Or find it via the Personal section and steal it back."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1794996675/Jason_Duval_07.jpg",
      "text_message_id": 57
    },
    "b0dd9d0bd0": {
      "id": "b0dd9d0bd0",
      "created": 1795068629.193738,
      "headline": "GTA 6 Weapon Ownership: How to Keep Your Favorite Guns",
      "url": "https://www.gamesradar.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-weapon-ownership-explained/",
      "source": "GamesRadar+",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068622/gta-bot/b0dd9d0bd0-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068622/gta-bot/b0dd9d0bd0-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068623/gta-bot/b0dd9d0bd0-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068624/gta-bot/b0dd9d0bd0-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068626/gta-bot/b0dd9d0bd0-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068628/gta-bot/b0dd9d0bd0-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Lost your favorite rifle in GTA 6? Weapon ownership is probably why. 🔫\n\nGuns you buy or get from a mission are yours to keep. Guns grabbed off enemies or from the world are only temporary, and you lose them if you're Wasted or Busted. Swipe for the full breakdown.\n\nWhich gun would you never leave behind?\n\nSource: GamesRadar\n\n#GTA6 #GTAVI #GrandTheftAutoVI #RockstarGames #Leonida #JasonAndLucia #GTA6Tips #GTA6Guide #AmmuNation #Gaming",
      "alt_text": "Graphic with the headline 'GTA 6 Weapon Ownership: How to Keep Your Favorite Guns' in The Leonida Daily style.",
      "score": 7,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "GUIDE",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "Owned vs unowned weapons",
          "text": "GTA 6 splits guns into two groups. Owned weapons are bought at Ammu-Nation or given to you by a character in a mission. Everything else you pick up is unowned."
        },
        {
          "title": "Keeping your owned guns",
          "text": "Buy a weapon with Pocket Cash or BuckMe and both Jason and Lucia get a copy. Each of them has to modify and equip it separately. Dropped owned guns can be recovered from your car's trunk or an Ammu-Nation locker."
        },
        {
          "title": "Unowned guns don't last",
          "text": "Weapons dropped by enemies or found lying around can't be recovered or modified. If you get Wasted or Busted, they're gone for good."
        },
        {
          "title": "Unique variants and new stock",
          "text": "Look for a golden gun icon on the minimap to find Unique Weapon Variants. They can't be modified, but they unlock permanently for both characters. Buying more guns also expands Ammu-Nation's stock."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1794996743/Jason_and_Lucia_13.jpg",
      "text_message_id": 63
    },
    "5535f1e6f1": {
      "id": "5535f1e6f1",
      "created": 1795077639.7017546,
      "headline": "GTA 6 Classic Controls: How to Switch Back to GTA 5 Feel",
      "url": "https://www.gamesradar.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-classic-controls/",
      "source": "GamesRadar+",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795077614/gta-bot/5535f1e6f1-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795077614/gta-bot/5535f1e6f1-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795077615/gta-bot/5535f1e6f1-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795077616/gta-bot/5535f1e6f1-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795077616/gta-bot/5535f1e6f1-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795077617/gta-bot/5535f1e6f1-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Muscle memory fighting you in Leonida? 🎮 There's a fix.\n\nGTA 6 launches with a new default control scheme, but you can switch to a Classic scheme that feels closer to GTA 5. Open the Options/Menu button, head to Settings and change the scheme. The default HUD is also more dynamic, and you can adjust that in Settings too.\n\nAre you sticking with the new controls or going Classic?\n\nSource: GamesRadar+\n\n#GTA6 #GrandTheftAutoVI #GTA #Leonida #RockstarGames #GTA6Tips #GTA6Guide #GTA5 #GamingNews #VideoGames",
      "alt_text": "Graphic with the headline 'GTA 6 Classic Controls: How to Switch Back to GTA 5 Feel' in The Leonida Daily style.",
      "score": 8,
      "reel_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/video/upload/v1795077638/gta-bot/5535f1e6f1-reel.mp4",
      "category": "GUIDE",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "How to turn on Classic controls",
          "text": "Press the Options/Menu button on your controller and go to Settings. There you can switch from the default scheme to the Classic control scheme, which gets you closer to the GTA 5 experience."
        },
        {
          "title": "What's different by default",
          "text": "In the new default scheme, running sits on L3/LS, while X/A is now jump. Melee has moved to Square/X. That's why GTA 5 veterans may feel thrown at first."
        },
        {
          "title": "Check the Dynamic HUD too",
          "text": "The default HUD hides non-essential info. Press down on the D-pad to bring up the minimap, bank balances, and health, stamina and focus bars. You can toggle all of these in Settings."
        },
        {
          "title": "More options to tweak",
          "text": "By default, you hold down on the D-pad and use L1/LB and R1/RB to cycle nearby tasks and locations and set destinations. You can also change how you interact with citizens from your car."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1794996648/Vice_City_24.jpg",
      "text_message_id": 99
    },
